<article class="env-lemma" id="04HJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04HJ">Lemma <span data-tag="04HJ">41.17.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a finite unramified morphism of schemes. Let $s \in S$. There exists an étale neighbourhood $(U, u) \to (S, s)$ and a finite disjoint union decomposition </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  X_ U = \coprod \nolimits _ j V_ j  \]
</div>
  <p> such that each $V_ j \to U$ is a closed immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $X \to S$ is finite the fibre over $s$ is a finite set $\{ x_1, \ldots , x_ n\} $ of points of $X$. Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/04HI" data-tag="04HI">41.17.2</a> to this set (a finite morphism is separated, see Morphisms, Section <a href="/tag/01WG" data-tag="01WG">29.45</a>). The image of $W$ in $U$ is a closed subset (as $X_ U \to U$ is finite, hence proper) which does not contain $u$. After removing this from $U$ we see that $W = \emptyset $ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>